question:
A Zomato SDE off-campus Round 1 (CS fundamentals, DSA and a resume deep-dive, which included multithreading and concurrency work) asked:

- the difference between a **thread and a process**, their advantages and when to use each;
- **inter-process communication (IPC)**: shared memory, pipes, message queues, semaphores and mutexes;
- the **thread lifecycle**: new, runnable, blocked, waiting, timed waiting and terminated;
- **multiprocessing vs multithreading**.
